    // LORE §4 gardener's lines (ART-SPEC 8.4: Intro banner, replaces "Get ready") and the ending line
    "level.1-1.intro": "The spring has stopped. Something is moving in the veg patch. Pebble Pod first.",
    "level.1-2.intro": "Dewcup says it can help gather water, as long as nobody wakes it.",
    "level.1-3.intro": "The stump by the door says it'll hold them off. It looks more nervous than me.",
    "level.1-4.intro": "The orchard is dry too. The ones wearing pots are what I never got round to planting.",
    "level.1-5.intro": "Thin ones run fast. Frostpod left the north corner on one condition: I never say \"hot\".",
    "level.1-6.intro": "They've learned to pole-vault. Good news: Thornmat has been itching to trip someone.",
    "level.1-7.intro": "Fence boards walked in on their own. The boiler-room onion is extra grumpy today. Good.",
    "level.1-8.intro": "Seeds from the baskets sprout where they land. I can't tell if that's good or bad.",
    "level.1-9.intro": "The biggest ones from the gourd trellis are coming too. Snapmaw says it's hungry.",
    "level.1-10.intro": "Sunlantern spoke at last. It says it remembers the sound of the spring.",
    "ending.line": "The lantern light reached the crack in the floor, and a root stirred. The spring is still dry, but the Rootmother is awake.",
